lesson: 116
title: The average of a few scores
stars: 0
explain: The average shares the total out evenly: add all the scores, then divide by how many scores there are.
explain: Scores 7, 9 and 11: the total is 27, there are 3 scores, so the average is 27 / 3 = 9.
explain: For four scores divide by 4: 6, 8, 10 and 12 make 36, and 36 / 4 = 9.
vars: a=name m=8..20 e=0..6 f=1..6 g=0..6
need: m - e + f - g >= 1
need: e != f
answer: m
exercise: {a} scored {m+e}, {m-f} and {m-e+f} points in three games. What is {a.his} average score?
exercise: In three tests {a} got {m-f}, {m+e} and {m-e+f} marks. What is the average mark?
exercise: {a} scored {m+e}, {m-f}, {m+g} and {m-e+f-g} points in four games. What is the average score?
exercise: Four children read {m-f}, {m+g}, {m+e} and {m-e+f-g} pages. On average, how many pages did each child read?
exercise: What is the average of {m+e}, {m-e+f} and {m-f}?
exercise: The average of four numbers: {m+g}, {m-f}, {m-e+f-g} and {m+e}. What is it?
test: Three friends caught {m-e+f}, {m+e} and {m-f} fish. If they shared the fish out evenly, how many would each friend get?
test: {a}'s team won {m+e} points on Monday, {m-f} on Tuesday, {m+g} on Wednesday and {m-e+f-g} on Thursday. Find the average number of points a day.
test: {a} jumped {m-f} cm, then {m-e+f} cm, then {m+e} cm. How far was the average jump, in cm?
test: The temperatures on four days were {m+g}, {m+e}, {m-f} and {m-e+f-g} degrees. What was the average temperature?
exercise: {a} from Texas scored {m-f}, {m+e} and {m-e+f} points in three games. What was the average?
exercise: Find the mean of {m-f}, {m-e+f} and {m+e}.
exercise: The three test marks are {m+e}, {m-e+f} and {m-f}. What is the average mark?
exercise: In four rounds of a quiz in Belfast, {a} got {m+g}, {m-e+f-g}, {m+e} and {m-f} points. What is {a.his} average per round?
exercise: Four bags hold {m-f}, {m+e}, {m+g} and {m-e+f-g} sweets. If the sweets were shared out equally among the bags, how many would each bag have?
exercise: What is the average of these four numbers: {m-e+f-g}, {m+e}, {m-f}, {m+g}?
exercise: {a} in Canberra ran {m+e}, {m-f} and {m-e+f} laps on three days. On average, how many laps did {a.he} run each day?
exercise: Three classes in Toronto collected {m-e+f}, {m-f} and {m+e} cans. What is the average number of cans per class?
test: Over three days {a} picked {m+e}, {m-e+f} and {m-f} strawberries in Kent. How many strawberries is that per day on average?
test: Four friends in Auckland have {m-f}, {m+g}, {m-e+f-g} and {m+e} marbles. If they put them together and shared them evenly, how many would each get?
test: The scores in three rounds were {m-e+f}, {m-f} and {m+e}. What is the mean score?
test: {a} measured the rainfall on four days: {m+e}, {m+g}, {m-f} and {m-e+f-g} mm. What was the average rainfall a day in mm?
test: Add {m+g}, {m-f}, {m+e} and {m-e+f-g}, then divide the sum by 4. What do you get?
test: Three shelves hold {m-f}, {m+e} and {m-e+f} books. How many books would be on each shelf if they were spread out evenly?
exercise: {a} got {m+e}, {m-f}, {m-e+f} in 3 games. average?
exercise: {a} scored {m+e}, {m-f+1} — no wait, {m-f} — and {m-e+f}. average score
